 "reviewHtml": "<div><p>“I’m all about beauty—but with some sense of ruggedness and adventure,” said Lela Rose. Right on cue, a model waltzed into her showroom wearing a hand-embroidered, lace-hemmed linen dress from the spring 2027 collection that exemplified that fusion. While elegant and formfitting, one could tell it was an outfit you could still be the life and soul of the party in.</p><p>Though the juxtaposition of humble fabric and high-touch embellishment felt fresh, the designer noted that the idea of ornate linen gowns actually harks back to her very first bridal collection in the early aughts: “Romantic, rustic, revisited,” she said with a laugh.</p><p>Three decades in, figuring out new ways to Lela Rose–ify a fabric remains top of mind. This season, light-as-air taffeta in shades of cornflower blue and lucky green was punched with tiny dots to resemble needlepoint, but in an unexpected and modern way. Motioning toward a perforated wall sconce of her own design that echoed the approach, Rose noted, “It reminds me of how I used to hole punch my mom’s luminaria when she was entertaining. When I’m in the showroom, I can really see the shared visual language everywhere.”</p><p>A tea-length linen frock also made for an ideal canvas to showcase three-dimensional floral detailing, as cut and frayed chiffon trimmed with beads transformed the unpretentious fabric into a scene-stealer. The same effect was utilized on the bodice of an ethereal tulle gown and to top a dance floor–ready black mini.</p><p>One thing notably less apparent in this offering were any nods to Westernwear, which tends to be Rose’s go-to since moving from Manhattan to Jackson Hole, Wyoming. But look closer and you could feel the ever-present ode to Americana in the ribbon saddle stitching adorning the sleeve of a blazer.</p><p>Similarly, an all-navy ensemble looked like it was destined for the boardroom, yet it was actually tricked out with a whole detachable utility belt too—like a very chic tool kit to fill to your heart’s content. “Just a fun way to mix things up and make it your own,” Rose said. That’s one way to ensure her muse is always ready for her next adventure.</p></div>",
